      "text": [
        " سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرَّمِيَّةِ يَجِدُهَا صَاحِبُهَا فِي الْغَدِ أَ يَأْكُلُ مِنْهُ فَقَالَ إِنْ عَلِمَ أَنَّ رَمْيَتَهُ هِيَ الَّتِي قَتَلَتْهُ فَلْيَأْكُلْ مِنْ ذَلِكَ إِذَا كَانَ قَدْ سَمَّى ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Hammad, from Hareyz who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> was asked about the shot at (by an arrow), so its owner finds it in the morning. Can he eat from it?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘If he knows that it was his shooting which killed it, so let him eat from that when he had Named (<span class=\"iTxt\">Bismillah</span>)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from Hammad from Hariz who has said the following: “Once abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, was asked about the prey which his owner finds the next day; if he can use it for food. He (the Imam) said, ‘If he knows that it is the prey which he had killed, he can use it for food if he had mentioned the name of Allah.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
